{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks","id":1413063,"title":"Cheaper and easier to use artifacts - what breaks?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-11T11:13:56-07:00","id":1413063,"title":"Cheaper and easier to use artifacts - what breaks?","content":"So I'm having three ways to do the whole 'artifact' thing.<br /> <br /> There are the good stuff. These are the artifacts with great powers and evocations. Your lightning cutter. The bow that fires out countless arrows that murder demons and gods. The brass knuckles that can shatter stone like cardboard and cause an earthquake. Ranging from Artifact 1 to N/A.<br /> <br /> And then there's the normal stuff. It's the kind of thing you gloss over. Stuff like your equivalent to your winterbreath jars, your singing staffs, your pots that create porridge.<br /> <br /> And then there's the really low tech stuff. Barely artifacts, and never rising above Artifact 1. These can never have evocations, save for truly rare circumstances (bathing in the blood of a slain behemoth is a suitable justification to get one). They're basically normal stuff with some magical material infused into them, letting them get higher stats and having small things like 'no rusting' and 'a lot more durable'. But that's about it. Nothing magical about it. You'll won't get the power to get a staff that can spew out fire. This is at the very tip of what mortals can do. No artifact is cheap, and this kind of artifact can only be obtained at a price of Resources 4/5. Something that can bankrupt and entire city state or cause a large dip in the finances of kings. Either way, most richer kingdoms out in the Threshold have at least one or two of these. If a DB or a hero wants doesn't want to expend effort into getting a full blown, powerful artifact, then this is what they get.<br /> <br /> And then, last of all, you can commit wilpower to attune to artifacts, in lieu of Essence.<br /> <br /> So the question is this: <br /> <br /> What does this break? <br /> <br /> One thing I can see happening is that Exalts just stroll over, and then start making the 3rd, lower kind of artifact. Sure there aren't any evocations, but the stat boost when you give it to your mortal buddies or just sell it off to your mercenaries is something that can't be ignored. <br /> <br /> Another thing that can happen is that mortal NPCs suddenly get a far too huge boost in power because they spent willpower to be able to use that grand goremaul or whatever. In other words, the elite can now splatter a DB if they roll well enough and have a big enough hammer. <br /> <br /> On the upside, there's more stories now. At least now with normal humans being able to use artifacts, there's more potential for story seeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 09-11-2020, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T11:36:26-07:00","id":1413066,"title":"","content":"I'd caution against artifacts that have small dot ratings and little to no attunement, but still have the statistics of an artifact. That just seems like an easy way to load up on artifact everything without appreciating the miracle of it, which I personally find is a bit of a problem already.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, not everything magical in Exalted need be an artifact. There's ironwood, which is wood so strong if you try to cut it with an axe you'll just end up smashing your iron axe head, feathersteel, which is pretty much super aluminum-titanium, or chiaroscuro glass, which is glass so strong that you can clash a sword made of it with one made of steel and it won't shatter.<br /> <br /> There's also bushes with leaves of cold iron that burn fairies, and massive dandelion plants that carry messages on their floating seeds. A lot of those things aren't even that expensive, just region specific. Chiaroscuro glass doesn't need regular oiling or protection from rust or water, and in chiaroscuro they're pretty common. Buying one in the far west though, that might be a bit expensive, and also make any marine forces there super envious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T11:49:45-07:00","id":1413069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413066#post1413066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd caution against artifacts that have small dot ratings and little to no attunement, but still have the statistics of an artifact. That just seems like an easy way to load up on artifact everything without appreciating the miracle of it, which I personally find is a bit of a problem already.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, not everything magical in Exalted need be an artifact. There's ironwood, which is wood so strong if you try to cut it with an axe you'll just end up smashing your iron axe head, feathersteel, which is pretty much super aluminum-titanium, or chiaroscuro glass, which is glass so strong that you can clash a sword made of it with one made of steel and it won't shatter.<br /> <br /> There's also bushes with leaves of cold iron that burn fairies, and massive dandelion plants that carry messages on their floating seeds. A lot of those things aren't even that expensive, just region specific. Chiaroscuro glass doesn't need regular oiling or protection from rust or water, and in chiaroscuro they're pretty common. Buying one in the far west though, that might be a bit expensive, and also make any marine forces there super envious.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what do we call 'mildly magical stuff that's better than normal stuff'? <br /> <br /> Sub-artifacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T11:54:09-07:00","id":1413070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413069#post1413069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do we call 'mildly magical stuff that's better than normal stuff'? <br /> <br /> Sub-artifacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, although the weird thing is that not all of it is magical, even if it\u2019s fantastical. Like there\u2019s giant dinosaurs that piss opioid drugs, and they\u2019re not technically magic in exalted? Like they don\u2019t use charms or Essence or sorcery or anything to do it, it\u2019s just a fact of their biology. Creation just isn\u2019t hampered by real world physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T12:05:56-07:00","id":1413072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413070#post1413070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, although the weird thing is that not all of it is magical, even if it\u2019s fantastical. Like there\u2019s giant dinosaurs that piss opioid drugs, and they\u2019re not technically magic in exalted? Like they don\u2019t use charms or Essence or sorcery or anything to do it, it\u2019s just a fact of their biology. Creation just isn\u2019t hampered by real world physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like... I know that there's lots of weird stuff in Creation. That's why I'm trying to make it easier. <br /> <br /> There *should* be smiths who have created one final masterpiece of their entire mortal life (some Exalted from the sheer achievement of making one) that's better than any metal should be, moving beyond mere 'good steel' into 'fit for a hero', that shines with an inner light and cuts demons like burning sunlight. There *should* be demenses and manses who serve as the equivalent of oil fields, creating medicines and products that are magical, not created by Exalted charms or sorcery but simply due to the powers of their ingredients. <br /> <br /> There just ain't enough cool and fun stuff in Exalted. I'm fine with nitty and gritty on the ground. But the higher levels of government should at least have paintings that glow with luminescent light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T13:13:43-07:00","id":1413086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413072#post1413072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There *should* be smiths who have created one final masterpiece of their entire mortal life (some Exalted from the sheer achievement of making one) that's better than any metal should be, moving beyond mere 'good steel' into 'fit for a hero', that shines with an inner light and cuts demons like burning sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely sounds like an artifact, which mortals aren\u2019t completely barred from making, they just need special circumstances. In fact the Throne of the Scarlett Empress was crafted by a mortal in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413072#post1413072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There *should* be demenses and manses who serve as the equivalent of oil fields, creating medicines and products that are magical, not created by Exalted charms or sorcery but simply due to the powers of their ingredients.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be a thing, although there\u2019s a bit of a threshold past which it would probably become an artifact. Like clay that you wrap a wound in and it 100% prevents infection is probably just a fantastical thing, but clay that you can form into the shape of an amputated limb and slap it onto where that limb was to regrow it instantly is something akin to an artifact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413072#post1413072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There just ain't enough cool and fun stuff in Exalted. I'm fine with nitty and gritty on the ground. But the higher levels of government should at least have paintings that glow with luminescent light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, paint made from Wyld fireflies that glows in the dark is a weird creation thing that\u2019s possible and would just be expensive. <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: ohhh okay I see now, you mean now. Well one thing that breaks is that basically every DB out there will be sporting artifact weapons and armor, normally just the ones who are warriors would, and if you do something like jump Ledaal Kes he\u2019s just going to have exquisitely crafted blades and armor, now they\u2019re magic. The biggest winners here are probably the Dynasts of the Realm, and their mortal allies since they\u2019re the ones scooping all the wealth. The mortal/Exalt divide gets a bit smaller, but with charms the exalts still firmly on top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T13:40:34-07:00","id":1413092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413086#post1413086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: ohhh okay I see now, you mean now. Well one thing that breaks is that basically every DB out there will be sporting artifact weapons and armor, normally just the ones who are warriors would, and if you do something like jump Ledaal Kes he\u2019s just going to have exquisitely crafted blades and armor, now they\u2019re magic. The biggest winners here are probably the Dynasts of the Realm, and their mortal allies since they\u2019re the ones scooping all the wealth. The mortal/Exalt divide gets a bit smaller, but with charms the exalts still firmly on top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question. What changed?<br /> <br /> I'm serious. Isn't the biggest problems basically 'Every single daiklave is a great treasure with an entire story behind it' and 'oh yeah, every dragonblooded soldier has one'. Like, this is a Dragonblooded Dynast. His underwear and spectacles are probably artifacts. <br /> <br /> Yes, that's kinda the thing. Everyone with infrastructure and backup milks it for all its worth, getting even more money and power and infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-11T14:25:38-07:00","id":1413104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413063-cheaper-and-easier-to-use-artifacts-what-breaks?p=1413092#post1413092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm serious. Isn't the biggest problems basically 'Every single daiklave is a great treasure with an entire story behind it' and 'oh yeah, every dragonblooded soldier has one'. Like, this is a Dragonblooded Dynast. His underwear and spectacles are probably artifacts. .</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not actually true, at least in third edition. If you go through the Princes of the Earth section in What Fore Has Wrought and Heirs to the Shogunate many characters don\u2019t have artifact weapons OR armor at all. Berit, 200+ year old daughter of the Empress? She\u2019s got artifact weapons and armor. Cathak Cainen, House matriarch for House Cathak, oh yeah, he\u2019s got them.<br /> <br /> Amon Mora, household head for the Imperial Palace? Nope. Cynis Cogen, 200+ year old reformed playboy monk? Nope there either. Ragara Benoru, leader of the bloody scythe rebellion and now magistrate of the Realm, she has an artifact gun but mundane chain shirt. Ledaal Kes just has mundane knives and no armor, but Sesus Nexeggar has both.<br /> <br /> Now, they\u2019re Dynasts, when Benoru has a mundane chain shirt that could easily be a silvered iron shirt that gleams in the sun, and has precious metal threads embroidered around the edge of each cuff. It may even have some minor really low level magic like rust prevention, see the Exceptional Weapons and Equipment section in the corebook. It\u2019s just not forged from the bones of a demon and quenched in the icy waters of a demense the northwest sea to give it supernatural resistance to attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}